DreamWidgetBlueprint:LastGoodPropVariables {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetBlueprint:LastGoodPropVariables
    src   "The `props` variables, `events` dispatchers and hidden anonymous-widget variable names of the last compile that\nread this asset's .dui into a hierarchy -- LastGoodResourceVariables' reason, for the class members the file\ndeclares beside its resources. A file that stops parsing keeps the previous hierarchy, and that hierarchy's\nbindings read these props, its emit handlers call these dispatchers and its unnamed widgets need their variables\nhidden; without them every one of those fails with an error pointing away from the one mistake in the file.\nEmpty for an asset that names no .dui."
    text  "上一次编译中将此资源的.dui读取为层级结构的`props`变量、`events`调度器和隐藏的匿名控件变量名，\n这是LastGoodResourceVariables的用途，即文件在其资源旁声明的类成员。停止解析的文件会保留先前的层级结构，而该层级结构的\n绑定会读取这些props，其emit处理程序会调用这些调度器，其未命名控件需要隐藏各自的变量；\n如果没有它们，上述每一项都会失败，并报出一个指向别处的错误，\n而不是文件中的那个错误。\n未指定任何.dui的资源为空。"
    state machine
}

DreamWidgetBlueprint:LastGoodResourceVariables {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetBlueprint:LastGoodResourceVariables
    src   "The `resources` class variables of the last compile that read this asset's .dui into a hierarchy.\n\nA compile whose file does not parse -- or cannot be read, or builds nothing -- keeps the previous\nhierarchy, and declares these again with it: the Blueprint compiler empties every generated variable\nbefore a compile declares its own, so the class would otherwise lose every resource, and every graph\nnode reading one would fail with an error pointing away from the one mistake in the file. Saved, so\na file that stopped parsing while the editor was closed still compiles with them. Empty for an asset\nthat names no .dui."
    text  "上次编译时从该资产的.dui读取层级的`resources`类变量。\n\n若某次编译的文件无法解析——或无法读取，或未构建出任何内容——则会保留先前的\n层级，并随之再次声明这些变量：蓝图编译器会在编译声明自己的变量之前清空所有\n生成的变量，因此类否则会失去每一个资源，而每个读取其中之一的图表\n节点都会失败，并给出一个指向别处的错误，而真正的问题只是文件中的那一处错误。此项会被保存，因此\n即使文件在编辑器关闭期间停止解析，它仍能带着这些变量完成编译。对于不指定\n任何.dui的资产，此项为空。"
    state machine
}

DreamWidgetBlueprint:PropertyBindings {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetBlueprint:PropertyBindings
    src   "Property bindings as authored. The compiler resolves each into the class's copy, and reports\nthe ones it cannot -- so a binding that stops making sense (the widget renamed, the function\ndeleted, the setter's type changed) surfaces on the next compile rather than at runtime."
    text  "按创作内容保存的属性绑定。编译器会将每个绑定解析到类的副本中，并报告\n无法解析的那些——因此，一个不再成立的绑定（控件被重命名、函数被\n删除、设置器的类型发生变化）会在下次编译时暴露出来，而不是在运行时。"
    state machine
}

DreamWidgetBlueprint:ViewModelSlots {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetBlueprint:ViewModelSlots
    src   "The `viewmodels` entries of this asset's .dui, as its last read declared them: variable, class and where the object\ncomes from. Rewritten by every compile that parses the file -- empty when it has no `viewmodels` block -- and left\nalone by one that does not (the variables of the last good read are declared again with the hierarchy it kept),\nand by an asset that names no .dui at all. The compiler hands it to the generated class\n(UDreamWidgetGeneratedClass::SetViewModelSlots), which the run time fills at Initialize."
    text  "该资产.dui中的`viewmodels`条目，按其上次读取时的声明：变量、类以及对象的\n来源。每次解析该文件的编译都会重写它——若没有`viewmodels`块则为空——而无法解析的编译\n会保持原样（上次成功读取的变量会随其保留的层级一起再次声明），\n完全不指定.dui的资产也是如此。编译器会把它交给生成的控件类\n（UDreamWidgetGeneratedClass::SetViewModelSlots），由运行时在Initialize时填充这些插槽。"
    state machine
}

DreamWidgetBlueprint:WidgetTree {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetBlueprint:WidgetTree
    src   "The hierarchy being authored. Never handed to instances directly; the compiler duplicates it."
    text  "正在创作的层级。不会直接交给实例；编译器会复制它。"
    state machine
}

DreamWidgetDesignerData {
    at    Source/DreamGUIEditor/Public/DreamWidgetBlueprint.h#DreamWidgetDesignerData
    src   "What the designer remembers about one authored hierarchy, as opposed to what the hierarchy IS.\n\nThe prefab kept the same set in FDreamUIPrefabDataForPrefabEditor, keyed by the GUIDs its helper\nobject handed out. There are no GUIDs here: a widget is identified by its object FName, which is\nwhat the class archetype and every instance preserve, and which is therefore already the key the\ntemplate-to-preview correspondence runs on. Two keys for the same thing is how they drift.\n\nGrid snapping and the overlays are deliberately NOT here -- those are per-author preferences and\nlive in UDreamUIDesignerSettings (EditorPerProjectUserSettings). What stays on the asset is what\ndescribes the hierarchy itself: how big its canvas is, and which of its widgets are put away."
    text  "设计器针对某个已创作层级所记住的内容，而非该层级本身。\n\n旧的prefab把同一组数据保存在FDreamUIPrefabDataForPrefabEditor中，以其辅助\n对象分配的GUID为键。这里没有GUID：控件由其对象FName标识，而这是\n类原型和每个实例都会保留的，因此它已经是模板到预览对应关系所使用的键。\n同一事物用两个键，正是它们发生偏差的原因。\n\n网格吸附和叠加层有意不放在这里——那些是每位作者的个人偏好，\n位于UDreamUIDesignerSettings（EditorPerProjectUserSettings）中。留在资产上的是\n描述层级本身的内容：其画布有多大，以及它的哪些控件被收起。"
    state machine
}

